    "source_ref": "q-71173",
    "original_problem": "$\\int 2+\\frac{1}{{y}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y=$",
    "original_solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2+\\frac{1}{{y}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int 1\\,\\text{d}y+\\int {y}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\int {y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y+\\int {y}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{{y}^{0+1}}{0+1}\\right)+\\frac{{y}^{-5+1}}{-5+1}+C \\\\  & =2y+\\frac{{y}^{-4}}{-4}+C \\\\  & =2y-\\frac{1}{4{y}^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
